# Phase Three — Final Brainstorm

The Awtsmoos renews the frame, yet truth persists through every scene;
Awtsmoos.com should hold one portable movie covenant, with many render vessels bright and clean.

## Final architecture image
Picture a vertical stack rather than a merger:

**Intent**
User prompt, local JSON, imported app project, or template.

**Canonical movie protocol**
Versioned normalized document + validation + capability catalog + timeline + feature inventory.

**Procedural asset intent**
Stable declarative requests that resolve through existing Awtsmoos Procedural Core generators and caches.

**Resolved semantic frame**
At time `t`, the engine identifies scene, local time, active layers, interpolated properties, camera intent, audio/caption cues, and asset readiness.

**Compositing adapters**
3D render surface beneath optional 2D overlay render surface. Apps may bind additional source types.

**Studio persona**
Animator, Nesher, Video Editor, Mitzvah Studio, and Awtsmoos Studio each expose a different editing experience and supported feature profile over the same protocol.

**Export provider**
Frame clock and compositing feed an actual encoder/provider where available.

## What belongs in Procedural Core
- canonical movie semantics if no equivalent canonical module has just landed;
- capability catalog and validation;
- movie asset intent bridge to existing generators;
- pure timeline/time/interpolation utilities;
- renderer-neutral feature inventory;
- generic adapters only when they do not depend on one app's UI/runtime.

## What does not belong in Procedural Core
- studio panels and toolbars;
- NLE-specific interaction state;
- browser recording UI;
- one app's export queue UX;
- remote AI provider credentials or transport;
- direct ownership of every possible Three/Canvas host.

## What belongs in shared Awtsmoos UI
- safe JSON recipe normalization;
- DOM creation and attribute policy;
- named action dispatch;
- state reads and typed input payloads;
- keyed lists and conditionals;
- custom mount slots;
- mobile-first studio shell helpers/tokens.

## What Awtsmoos Studio must prove
It must be more than a landing page. It should:
- load the canonical three-minute movie;
- show validated feature/duration status;
- accept/edit/import JSON;
- report validation errors in useful paths;
- play/pause/seek from the canonical clock;
- display a scene navigator/timeline;
- render 2D tutorial/infographic content;
- render real 3D/procedural content through the available adapter;
- composite overlays;
- expose asset readiness/errors;
- expose export capability and perform real export if the provider/runtime supports it;
- work at a phone viewport first.

## What “all existing apps unified” must mean
Not identical UI. Not one giant app. It means:
- they can understand/import/export or delegate canonical movie documents through a real imported adapter;
- their advertised capabilities are discoverable;
- they do not each maintain a competing core schema for the same universal concepts;
- specialized local concepts remain local extensions;
- unsupported canonical nodes survive round-trip when possible rather than being silently destroyed.

## Proof movie as architecture torture test
Twelve 15-second scenes produce exact duration while permitting many internal beats. The movie should reuse actor and asset IDs across scenes, use both semantic infographic nodes and lower-level shapes, include deterministic particle seeds, use camera target IDs, and combine 3D scene surfaces with 2D annotations. That makes the fixture a regression suite rather than a decorative demo.

## Fallback hierarchy
1. Use real shared procedural/render/export capability discovered in repository.
2. If a particular app cannot render a node, delegate to shared preview adapter.
3. If a browser feature is unavailable, degrade visibly and preserve data.
4. Never substitute a fake claim for unavailable capability.

## Concurrency discipline
Another agent may land a better version between planning and coding. The correct action is to inspect, merge concepts, and build the missing layer. Novelty is not the goal; a coherent repository is.

Final brainstorm conclusion: let one movie protocol become the inner light, procedural core become the foundry, Awtsmoos UI become the vessel-maker, and every studio remain a distinct instrument in the same orchestra.
